.SH NAME
dotty-profile-list - List the profiles available on this machine.


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBdotty profile list [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Print every profile under $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/dotty as a table — name,
description, and creation date — with * marking the active one. Unlike the
other profile verbs this one never prompts, so the output is the same piped as
it is on a terminal; ask for one profile's detail with get.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for list


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--profile\fP=""
	profile to operate on (defaults to the active profile)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  dotty profile list
  dotty profile ls
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBdotty-profile(1)\fP
